infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title CommonJS vs ESM: why one import shipped a whole library
  desc Tree-shaking only proves an export unused on static ES modules — CommonJS forces the bundler to keep everything
  compares
    - label CommonJS — import _ from "lodash"
      children
        - label ~24 KB shipped for one helper
          desc Importing just isArray drags the entire library
        - label Exports computed at runtime
          desc module.exports is assembled dynamically, so the bundler can't prove which keys you use
        - label Not tree-shakeable
          desc Unprovable means every unused export is kept to be safe
    - label ESM — import debounce from "lodash-es"
      children
        - label ~46 bytes shipped for one helper
          desc Only the single function you actually imported
        - label Static import / export
          desc Analyzable at build time, so the bundler proves the rest is dead
        - label Tree-shakeable
          desc Unused exports dropped — deep imports (lodash/debounce) work too
theme
  palette #f43f5e #10b981
